# inkpaperUI (working name)

A line-art UI kit for Tailwind CSS v4: ink outlines on warm paper, one red accent. A sister to
`../gamifiedUI`; the design brief is `docs/BRIEF.md` and is the source of truth for the look.

## Layout

- `packages/inkpaperui-css`: tokens (`src/tokens.css`), type (`src/base.css`), one file per
  component in `src/components`, each imported from `src/index.css`.
- `packages/inkpaperui-icons`: icons as stroke paths on a 24px grid in `icons.mjs`; `npm run build`
  writes `src/index.css`, `svg/` and `icons.json`. Never edit the generated files.
- `demo`: one page on port 5395 (5391 to 5394 belong to 掃街, Taste Quest and the gamifiedUI demo).

## Rules

- Class names, modifiers and markup mirror gamifiedUI (`gx-btn-primary` there is
  `ip-btn-primary` here), so a game can switch kits by swapping imports. Check gamifiedUI's
  component before naming a new one; icons share gamifiedui-icons' names where both have one.
- Colours live only in `tokens.css`; components use the `--color-ip-*` tokens. Text colours must
  reach 4.5:1 on paper; the bright accent is for lines, fills and large type only.
- Outlines are CSS borders with the uneven `--ip-shape-*` radii; pen strokes (underlines, ticks)
  are SVG masks over a colour, drawn in black because they are masks.
- Every state is shown by more than colour: dashed lines for disabled, an icon and words for
  danger. Focus is the 3px red ring, on keyboard focus.
- Motion uses the `--ip-motion-*` tokens, which drop to 0 under reduced motion.
- Demo text goes through the three locale tables in `demo/src/main.ts` (en, zh-Hant Cantonese,
  zh-Hans with mainland words).
- Style: single quotes, semicolons, 2-space indent, trailing commas; comments explain why, never
  what.
- Done means `npm test` and `npm run build` pass and the demo is checked in a browser.
- Public repo `carsonhung/inkpaperUI` (Apache-2.0); every push to `main` deploys the demo to
  GitHub Pages at /inkpaperUI/. Commit messages are one plain sentence; never commit `.env`.
  Don't commit, push or publish to npm without the user's go-ahead.
